6. GDPR (UK) COMPLIANCE
   The Software is designed to assist Blake UK Ltd in operating a customer
   support service and includes technical measures to support compliance with
   the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection
   Act 2018. These measures include:

   a) DATA MINIMISATION
      The chat widget collects only data strictly necessary for session
      continuity and support purposes: a hashed IP address, the page URL
      visited, and the content of customer chat messages.

   b) LAWFUL BASIS
      Personal data is processed on the basis of legitimate interests
      (Article 6(1)(f) UK GDPR) to enable customer support, and on the
      basis of consent where the customer voluntarily initiates a chat.

   c) DATA RETENTION
      Chat session data and message logs are subject to retention controls
      configurable by the Data Controller (Blake UK Ltd). Tracking query
      data and personal data are deleted in accordance with the Controller's
      retention policy.

   d) SECURITY
      API keys are stored encrypted (AES-256-GCM). Admin access is
      protected by bcrypt-hashed passwords, CSRF tokens, rate limiting,
      and secure session cookies (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict).
      IP addresses stored in the system are hashed using SHA-256.

   e) DATA SUBJECT RIGHTS
      Blake UK Ltd, as Data Controller, is responsible for handling
      data subject requests (access, erasure, rectification, objection)
      under UK GDPR Articles 15-22. The Software does not automatically
      process such requests; they must be handled by the Controller.

   f) DATA PROCESSOR
      If this Software is deployed by a third party on behalf of
      Blake UK Ltd, that third party acts as a Data Processor and must
      enter into a Data Processing Agreement with Blake UK Ltd as
      required by UK GDPR Article 28.

   g) INTERNATIONAL TRANSFERS
      The Software uses the Google Gemini API (Google LLC, USA). Blake
      UK Ltd is responsible for ensuring an appropriate transfer mechanism
      (such as Standard Contractual Clauses or the UK-US Data Bridge)
      is in place before processing personal data through this service.

   h) COOKIES AND TRACKING
      The chat widget uses sessionStorage (not persistent cookies) to
      maintain session continuity. No third-party tracking or analytics
      are built into the Software. The Data Controller is responsible
      for ensuring any cookie consent requirements on the host website
      are satisfied before the widget script is loaded.

   i) PRIVACY NOTICE
      Blake UK Ltd must maintain a Privacy Notice that describes the
      processing activities enabled by this Software, accessible to
      customers prior to or at the point of data collection.

   j) DATA PROTECTION OFFICER
      Blake UK Ltd should assess whether appointment of a DPO is required
      under UK GDPR Article 37 based on the nature and scale of processing.

